# =============================================================================
# Termi — Electron App (.env.example)
#
# HOW ENV VARS WORK IN ELECTRON:
#
#   Development  — Electron reads the monorepo root .env (../../.env from this file).
#                  Use that file for all configuration during development.
#
#   Packaged app — Electron reads termi.config.json from the OS user-data directory:
#                    macOS:   ~/Library/Application Support/Termi/termi.config.json
#                    Windows: %APPDATA%\Termi\termi.config.json
#                  See termi.config.json.example in this directory for the format.
#
# The variables listed here are ones specific to the Electron shell itself.
# Variables needed by the bundled Next.js server and gateway are documented in
#   apps/web/.env.example     — web / Next.js vars
#   apps/gateway/.env.example — gateway vars
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# ELECTRON-SPECIFIC  (optional)
# =============================================================================

# Force development mode even in a packaged build.
# Useful for debugging a production build without disabling packaging.
# ELECTRON_DEV=1

# Override the default app URL injected into the bundled Next.js process.
# Only needed if you run the app on a non-default port or hostname.
# Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:22080
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:22080

#ALLOWED_ORIGINS, DATABASE_URL, DB_HOST, DB_NAME, DB_PASSWORD, DB_USER, DOTENV_CONFIG_DEBUG, DOTENV_CONFIG_QUIET, DOTENV_KEY, ELECTRON_DEV, GATEWAY_HOST, GATEWAY_JWT_SECRET, GATEWAY_PORT, GUACD_HOST, GUACD_PORT, NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL, SHELL, WS_NO_BUFFER_UTIL, WS_NO_UTF_8_VALIDATE